+(duration)=
+
+### Duration
+
+The {class}`Duration` type converts a duration into a
+{class}`datetime.timedelta`. A duration is either a whole number of seconds,
+like `120`, or one or more `<integer><unit>` groups, like `1h30m`. The units
+are `d`, `h`, `m`, and `s`, for days, hours, minutes, and seconds. Each unit
+may appear at most once and in that order, with no spaces between groups. Units
+are case-insensitive, so `45S` is the same as `45s`.
+
+```{eval-rst}
+.. click:example::
+
+    @click.command()
+    @click.option("--timeout", type=click.Duration(), default="30s")
+    def wait(timeout):
+        click.echo(f"Waiting {timeout.total_seconds():g} seconds")
+
+.. click:run::
+
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=1h30m'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=90'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=30m1h'])
+    println()
+    invoke(wait, args=['--help'])
+```
+
+```{versionadded} 8.6.0
+```
+
